   3.395421873418894*^9, 3.395607533950148*^9}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Recursive Processes", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3950050750221233`*^9, 3.3950050875924597`*^9}, {
  3.395422438918091*^9, 3.395422447760174*^9}, {3.3956077154382877`*^9, 
  3.395607719584688*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Background",
 FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395607835043456*^9, 3.3956078403865137`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
A major shift in the way physicists think can be traced to 1972, and for a \
curious reason. In that year Hewlett-Packard introduced the HP-35, the first \
programmable calculator. It rapidly acquired the status of a cult object.  \
\"HP-35 Clubs\" appeared in scientific centers around the world. Physicists \
began to look forward to such dreary events as faculty meetings as \
opportunities to twiddle with their HP-35s, started sharing tricks (slowly\
\[LongDash]those were the days before e-mail), and interest was awakened in \
some mathematical phenomena that on first encounter seemed \
strange\[LongDash]the seeds of much that came after.   \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tFor example: Select a number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " between 0 and 1, and repeatedly hit the Cos key. What you are thus \
computing is"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Ellipsis]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       SubscriptBox["x", "0"], "]"}], "]"}], "\[Ellipsis]"}], "]"}], "]"}],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It was observed that the output converged to 0.739085 ",
 StyleBox["independently of the value you had assigned to the \"seed\"",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ". This result is really not unexpected in the light of the following \
calculation "
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FindRoot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], "\[Equal]", "x"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", ".7"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", "0.7390851332151608`"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395607985563272*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "but is unforgettably impressive when done \"in the hand\". It can be \
phrased this way: ",
 StyleBox["iteration",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " of  "
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"map", ":", " ", "x"}],
   FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
  StyleBox["\[Rule]",
   FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}],
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox[" ",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox["yields",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox[" ",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox["0.739085",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox[" ",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox["as",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox[" ",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], 
   StyleBox["a",
    FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], " ", 
   StyleBox["fixed",
    FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]], 
   StyleBox[" ",
    FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]], 
   StyleBox["point",
    FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tPeople tried other maps, and found that some yielded an ",
 StyleBox["alternating pair",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " of fixed points:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608096878018*^9, 3.396105825184524*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
  "a", ",", "b", ",", "a", ",", "b", ",", "a", ",", "b", ",", "a", ",", 
   "..."}], "Output"]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3956080759624567`*^9, 3.395608084701169*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Other maps yielded still more complicated ",
 StyleBox["patterns after many iterations",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 ". Some parameterized families of maps"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"parameterizedmap", ":", " ", "x"}], "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["f", "\[Lambda]"], "[", "x", "]"}]}],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]]], "Output"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "were found upon iteration to possess the property that ",
 StyleBox["slight \[Lambda]-adjustment produces radical alteration of the \
asymptotic pattern",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 ".  And sometimes the asymptotic output appears to be patternless/random, \
even though the map itself contains no element of randomness\[Ellipsis]is \
\"deterministic;\" thus did the mathematical\[LongDash]also (as it develops) \
ubiquitous physical\[LongDash]phenomenon of \"deterministic chaos\" come into \
focus. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395608229015059*^9, 3.3956082374426622`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tPhysicists soon learned to recognize instances/analogs of all of those \
phenomena in a wide range of physical problems. My job here will be to \
illustrate how ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " can be used to approach such subject matter\[LongDash]a subject matter \
that for the most part resists the techniques of classical analysis. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39560827263936*^9, 3.395608275588821*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395608292409066*^9, 3.395608292489352*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Basic Tools",
 FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395608302508604*^9, 3.395608307369673*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "No longer is it necessary to \"hit the Cos key many times.\" One ",
 StyleBox["can",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " do so\[LongDash]proceed"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "0.2", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["0.9800665778412416`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608382647284*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "%", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["0.5569672528096424`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608385066307*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "%", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["0.8488621656582708`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608387430781*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "%", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["0.660837551116615`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608389466476*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "%", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["0.7894784377668683`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608391739059*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "0.2", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395608421695305*^9, 3.395608426497241*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData["0.7894784377668683`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.39560843292304*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[LongDash]but ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " provides tools that do such things automatically: an informative \
introduction to this subject can be found by commanding"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3956086447011967`*^9, 3.3956087001283083`*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", 
  StyleBox["Nest",
   FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  StyleBox["\<\"\\!\\(\\*RowBox[{\\\"Nest\\\", \\\"[\\\", RowBox[{StyleBox[\\\
\"f\\\", \\\"TI\\\"], \\\",\\\", StyleBox[\\\"expr\\\", \\\"TI\\\"], \
\\\",\\\", StyleBox[\\\"n\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]}], \\\"]\\\"}]\\) gives an \
expression with \\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"f\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]\\) applied \
\\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"n\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]\\) times to \
\\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"expr\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]\\). \"\>", "MSG"], " ", 
  ButtonBox[
   StyleBox["\[RightSkeleton]", "SR"],
   Active->True,
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Nest"]}]], "Print", "PrintUsage",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608463644712*^9},
 CellTags->"Info3395583262-1714501"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and following the ",
 StyleBox["\[RightSkeleton]",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 ". Here we reproduce\[LongDash]with a single command\[LongDash]the \
calculation that we just did \"longhand\" "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3956087029559793`*^9, 3.395608719713077*^9}, {
  3.395676488891581*^9, 3.39567657110011*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "0.2", ",", "5"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.395608860012773*^9, {3.395676465148295*^9, 3.3956764689164658`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData["0.7894784377668683`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608867227086*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
and here we just as effortlessly extend the interation to depth 100:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395676591210546*^9, 3.395676629232473*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "0.2", ",", 
   StyleBox["100",
    FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3956088934566383`*^9, 3.395608894022923*^9}, 
   3.396138525638371*^9}],

Cell[BoxData["0.7390851332151607`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395608910471961*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

