}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395694574316081*^9, 3.395694574763852*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "   \[Bullet] the abrupt ",
 StyleBox["onset of chaos",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " (and its occasional\[LongDash]equally abrupt\[LongDash]disappearance);"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395694568105517*^9, 3.395694577419783*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "   \[Bullet] a cryptic ",
 StyleBox["universality",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395694579147635*^9, 3.395694594827057*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
These notions live not only in the world of mathematical abstraction; \
symptoms of them have been found to be all around us in the physical world, \
now that we have acquired eyes to see them.  They can be found in physics (in \
all of its flavors), biology, economics\[Ellipsis]and have become \
indispensable players in any modern conception of \"how the world works.\" \
\>", "Text"],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395694664266657*^9, 3.395694664316113*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Coupled Nonlinear ODEs with Chaotic Solutions", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39569471187107*^9, 3.3956947290739403`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
We are in the habit of considering the world\[LongDash]those parts of it of \
greatest interest to physicists\[LongDash]to be described not by iterated \
maps but by differential equations. It has only in fairly recent times come \
to be widely appreciated (though it was evident to Poincare already a century \
ago) that fairly simple systems of coupled ODEs can have wildly irregular \
solutions\[LongDash]solutions that depend very critically upon the prescribed \
initial conditions. I give two examples: \
\>", "Text"],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395700798639185*^9, 3.3957007987395763`*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Rikitake's  Model of Geomagnetic Field Reversal",
 FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39570081204462*^9, 3.395700831154664*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In 1958, T. Rikitake (Proc. Camb. Phil. Soc. ",
 StyleBox["54",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 89\[Dash]105) used a simple coupled disk dynamo system to model the \
generation of the earth's magnetic field (see \[Section]6.1 in S. Neil \
Rasband's ",
 StyleBox["Chaotic Dynamics of Nonlinear Systems",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (1990) for details; also the final pages of H. K. Moffatt, ",
 StyleBox["Magnetic Field  Generation in Electrically  Conducting Fluids",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (1978)).  He was led to the following system of coupled 1st order \
nonlinear ODEs: "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395700907719638*^9, 3.395700934989602*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[{
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Mu]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"y", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Alpha]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"u", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]]}], "Output"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox[
  RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ">", 
   RowBox[{"0", "  ", "and", "  ", "\[Alpha]"}], ">", 
   RowBox[{"0", "  ", "are", " ", "parameters"}]}],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.500008]]], "Output"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is easy enough for",
 StyleBox[" Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "to construct numerical solutions of such coupled ODEs.  Preliminary \
experimentation leads us to assign illustrative values of 1.0 and 2.7 to \
\[Mu] and \[Alpha], and initial values of 1.0, 0 and 0.5 to ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["y",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["u",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; we then obtain",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395701040659616*^9, 3.3957010588272963`*^9}, {
  3.395701090855076*^9, 3.395701091312216*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
  RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "u", ",", "t"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"rikitake", "=", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], 
         RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"y", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "2.7"}], 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"u", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], 
         RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "[", "0", "]"}], "\[Equal]", "1.0"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"y", "[", "0", "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u", "[", "0", "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0.5"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "u"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "200"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"MaxSteps", "\[Rule]", "6000"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395701733439595*^9, 3.395701736058292*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", 
     TagBox[
      RowBox[{"InterpolatingFunction", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.`", ",", "200.`"}], "}"}], "}"}], ",", "\<\"<>\"\>"}], 
       "]"}],
      False,
      Editable->False]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"y", "\[Rule]", 
     TagBox[
      RowBox[{"InterpolatingFunction", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.`", ",", "200.`"}], "}"}], "}"}], ",", "\<\"<>\"\>"}], 
       "]"}],
      False,
      Editable->False]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"u", "\[Rule]", 
     TagBox[
      RowBox[{"InterpolatingFunction", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.`", ",", "200.`"}], "}"}], "}"}], ",", "\<\"<>\"\>"}], 
       "]"}],
      False,
      Editable->False]}]}], "}"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3957011331876297`*^9, 3.395701743835956*^9}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["REMARK",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ": ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reported itself unable to do what we had commanded with the default 1000 \
",
 StyleBox["MaxSteps", "Input"],
 " value, so we increased it. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3957011638180637`*^9, 3.395701239305216*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395701284721355*^9, 3.3957012848292437`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How to display the numerical information which ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has now at its disposal? Rikitaki himself plotted"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], "/.", "%"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "200"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", "All"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395701322719522*^9}],

