Cell[TextData[{
 "The qualitative resemblance to results obtained from the (much less \
well-known) Rikitake model is striking. We again detect the scent of some \
kind of \"universality\" principle\[Ellipsis]in which connection we note that \
both systems are (not obviously, the way I have presented them) ",
 StyleBox["nonlinear forced dissipative",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " systems. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395704698783392*^9, 3.395704703056085*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "I will not pursue this rich topic, because to do so would risk being \
seduced by the physics, and our present assignment is simply to become \
acquainted with the utility of ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". So I leave the ",
 StyleBox["Poincare maps",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Liapunov exponents",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 ", etc. for you to explore on your own, if someday you are so inclined."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395704772427663*^9}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You will appreciate that DEs are like iterated maps, in that they tell the \
state point where to go, where to go, where to go\[Ellipsis] And that such \
rich structure as we have seen is exposed only by numerical analysis (which \
",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " takes in easy stride).  And the moral of it all: ",
 StyleBox["simple rules can have inexhaustibly complex consequences",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3957047932912493`*^9, 3.395704820980933*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395707586685525*^9, 3.3957075866910667`*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Fitting Curves to Data", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395707606034574*^9, 3.395707610441958*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3957076682671537`*^9, 3.395707668286353*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Preliminary Remarks",
 FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3957076803241453`*^9, 3.395707684283332*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
It is increasingly rare for your activity in the laboratory to be describable \
as \"hands-on\" production of \"raw data.\" For it has become commonplace for \
a computer (else built-in special-purpose software) to stand between you and \
the measurement device, interpreting your intentions to the device, and \
reporting back a pre-digested account of what the device has detected. Which \
is OK if the software works, and if you know the true meaning of its reports. \
\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
But occasionally you find yourself in the classical situation of \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3957077379271917`*^9}],

Cell["\<\
   \[Bullet] trying to make statistical sense of tabulated experimental data;\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395707775991325*^9, 3.3957077784050903`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
   \[Bullet] trying to make statistical sense of tabulated experimental data;\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395707781948843*^9, 3.395707783828671*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Concerning the first issue: ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is general purpose mathematical software, not a \"statistics engine.\" ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " does, however, come with elaborate built-in statistical capabilities\
\[LongDash]go to ",
 StyleBox["Documention Center",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", look at the box labeled",
 StyleBox[" Data Handling & Data Sources",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", then search for ",
 StyleBox["guide/Statistics",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " for basic information and tutorials\[LongDash]and many statistical \
packages add in various ways to that capability."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395707895256419*^9, 3.395707905762301*^9}, {
  3.395708737241331*^9, 3.3957087471780367`*^9}, {3.395708797734783*^9, 
  3.3957091078928423`*^9}}],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395709190060904*^9, 3.395709190070242*^9}}]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Importing Data",
 FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395709212464774*^9, 3.395709215990032*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is valuable in this connection to know ",
 StyleBox["how to import data",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " into ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". This is not difficult\[Ellipsis]the essential command being"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395709245185215*^9, 3.395709264236885*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", 
  StyleBox["Import",
   FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  StyleBox["\<\"\\!\\(\\*RowBox[{\\\"Import\\\", \\\"[\\\", StyleBox[\\\"\\\\\
\\\"\\\\!\\\\(\\\\*StyleBox[\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TI\\\\\\\"]\\\\)\\\\\
\\\"\\\", ShowStringCharacters->True], \\\"]\\\"}]\\) imports data from a \
file, returning a complete \\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"Mathematica\\\", FontSlant \
-> \\\"Italic\\\"]\\) version of it. \\n\\!\\(\\*RowBox[{\\\"Import\\\", \
\\\"[\\\", \
RowBox[{StyleBox[\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\!\\\\(\\\\*StyleBox[\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\",\\\\\
\\\"TI\\\\\\\"]\\\\)\\\\\\\"\\\", ShowStringCharacters->True], \\\",\\\", \
StyleBox[\\\"elements\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]}], \\\"]\\\"}]\\) imports the \
specified elements from a file.\\n\\!\\(\\*RowBox[{\\\"Import\\\", \\\"[\\\", \
RowBox[{StyleBox[\\\"\\\\\\\"http://\\\\!\\\\(\\\\*StyleBox[\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\
\",\\\\\\\"TI\\\\\\\"]\\\\)\\\\\\\"\\\",ShowStringCharacters->True], \
\\\",\\\", StyleBox[\\\"\[Ellipsis]\\\", \\\"TR\\\"]}], \\\"]\\\"}]\\) and \
\\!\\(\\*RowBox[{\\\"Import\\\", \\\"[\\\", \
RowBox[{StyleBox[\\\"\\\\\\\"ftp://\\\\!\\\\(\\\\*StyleBox[\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\"\
,\\\\\\\"TI\\\\\\\"]\\\\)\\\\\\\"\\\",ShowStringCharacters->True], \\\",\\\", \
StyleBox[\\\"\[Ellipsis]\\\", \\\"TR\\\"]}], \\\"]\\\"}]\\) imports from any \
accessible URL. \"\>", "MSG"], " ", 
  ButtonBox[
   StyleBox["\[RightSkeleton]", "SR"],
   Active->True,
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Import"]}]], "Print", "PrintUsage",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.395709279910755*^9},
 CellTags->"Info3395684079-6054747"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To demonstrate how this works, I have deposited a file named ",
 StyleBox["SedonaMorning.jpg",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " in the ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " Manuals folder on the Courses Server. To import that file, first write the \
incomplete command"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.395709442877942*^9, {3.3957101193921223`*^9, 3.395710149920045*^9}, {
   3.39573355842911*^9, 3.395733571407878*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Import", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39570970669433*^9, 3.395709778379211*^9}, {
   3.39570987833815*^9, 3.3957098801369333`*^9}, {3.39571006356569*^9, 
   3.395710079053342*^9}, 3.3957101139318333`*^9}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Then go to ",
 StyleBox["Insert > File Path\[Ellipsis]  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The \"Select a file\" window will open showing all accessible files, and at \
the bottom of which are found a ",
 StyleBox["Cancel",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.5, 0, 0.5]],
 " button and a ",
 StyleBox["Choose",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.5, 0, 0.5]],
 " button.  Select ",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Blossoms.jpg file and\[LongDash]with the cursor blinking at the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["\[Wedge]",
    FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]], TraditionalForm]]],
 " in the ",
 StyleBox["Import[ ]", "Input"],
 " command\[LongDash]hit the ",
 StyleBox["Choose",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.5, 0, 0.5]],
 " button: the desired file ",
 StyleBox["\"path\"", "Input",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.5]],
 " will be inserted between the square brackets, as shown below. Execute the \
command (i.e., hit \[EnterKey]) and an imported copy of the file will \
appear."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.395710157521821*^9, 3.395710213933888*^9}, {
  3.395710243942966*^9, 3.395710295822007*^9}, {3.395710375481473*^9, 
  3.395710451976101*^9}, {3.3957104823494463`*^9, 3.3957104912568502`*^9}, {
  3.3957105856316853`*^9, 3.3957106129164543`*^9}, {3.39571077287685*^9, 
  3.39571080050988*^9}, {3.395710873074588*^9, 3.395710903260758*^9}, {
  3.395710933348179*^9, 3.395710998658683*^9}, {3.395733179835908*^9, 
  3.395733405385623*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
